## Agentic usage — Cursor

**Pre-flight.** Objective specific · expected behavior known · relevant files identified · existing
pattern found · constraints listed · validation defined · cheapest capable model chosen · correct
tool for this stage · investigation or planning needed first · no other agent on the same problem ·
you can review the result · included Cursor requests accounted for · this portion could be done
outside the IDE. Several "no" answers → improve the task definition first.

**Prompt format.** Objective / Context / Current behavior / Expected behavior / Constraints /
Validation / Scope. Describe the outcome, not the activity; point at the existing pattern instead of
asking the agent to find it; state non-goals; give the validation commands; include what was tried
and why it failed. **Separate investigation from implementation** — investigate under "do not modify
files", review the findings, then implement.

**Plan Mode** before a change that: touches more than ~5 files; crosses app layers; has ambiguous
requirements; needs investigation before the solution is known; includes a migration; must stay
backward compatible; touches checkout, customer data, auth, payments or security; exceeds one
focused session; spans repositories; introduces a new architectural pattern; or would force several
assumptions. A plan of generic steps ("update the component") is not a plan.

**Running the agent.** One primary outcome per session; give the exact files, similar
implementations, tests, error output and AC — not the repo. **Stop the run early** when
the agent duplicates an existing utility, edits unrelated files, drops behavior unexplained, guesses
at an API, repeats a failed approach, widens scope unasked, rewrites a subsystem for a localized
bug, disables a test, hides type errors behind casts or ignores, changes dependencies, or continues
after a core assumption is disproved. Never send a bare "Continue": review what changed, then give a
specific next instruction or start a clean conversation. Before a second parallel agent: distinct
objective, not the same investigation, value that justifies it, capacity to review both. Stop agents
once useless.

**Data handling.** Never paste credentials, customer, personal or restricted data into a prompt, and
never enter restricted information into an unapproved system.

**Before the PR.** Review every changed file yourself, drop unrelated edits, run the tests / lint /
typecheck, validate the original AC, confirm no check was disabled, stop leftover agents. An agent's
claim that tests pass or the change is safe is not evidence. fnd already encodes the guidelines'
completion checklist — run `qa-feature-or-fix`, then `pre-commit-review`, and answer their findings
instead of redoing it.
